/// The `opener` interface provides a function to hand a URI to the system
/// outside the host application, so that whatever is arranged to deal with its
/// scheme takes it from there.
///
/// A host may have nothing to hand URIs to. That is not exceptional, and
/// callers are expected to carry on without.
interface opener {
    /// Hands a URI to whatever the system has arranged to deal with its
    /// scheme.
    ///
    /// * `uri`: The absolute URI to hand over.
    ///
    /// Returns whether the host passed it on.
    ///
    /// The host validates the URI and may reject it according to its policy,
    /// including because of its scheme or destination. A host must not hand
    /// over a URI it does not recognise as safe. An invalid or rejected URI
    /// returns `false`.
    ///
    /// A result of `true` indicates only that the URI left the host. It
    /// carries no information about what the system did with it, and no
    /// indication that it was seen. A result of `false` is not exceptional: a
    /// host with nothing to hand URIs to always returns it. A caller that
    /// needs the URI to be reached should fall back to presenting it and
    /// letting the person open it themselves.
    open: func(uri: string) -> bool;
}
